The conductor's rounds take 8 minutes and pass you by — two taps on the door, a bored hum on the downslope.
The cabin is orderly the way a stage set is orderly. Behind the writing case: a solicitor's letter — and the Vane household ledger, far from its shelf.
The Flyer hisses down at the border. A telegraph boy sprints the platform and puts a French telegram into Brack's white glove.
  (+1h) time passes.

