« 1:2 @ MARCH EXPLORE FIREBOX »
  (+1halfhour) You sift warm ash while Cole watches the shovel a shade too carefully.
14 minutes of sifting, well spent: a wax phonomotor cylinder, half-melted but intact, the lord's monogram on the brass case.
A thin smell of ash reaches the corridor: someone is feeding the firebox, and a ledger cover stamped VANE is curling in the flames.
  (+1h) time passes.

